# The presence of this file stops npm falling back to .gitignore when deciding
# what to pack. That fallback is a trap here: .gitignore excludes build/, which
# is exactly the directory that has to ship. The `files` whitelist in
# package.json is the real allowlist; this file only carves things back out.

# Test-only bundle. It re-exports the internals so the suite can exercise the
# built artifact rather than a second compilation of the source. It is not
# public API, it is not reachable through `exports`, and it should not add
# 67 KB to everyone's node_modules.
build/internal.mjs
build/internal.d.ts

node_modules
*.tgz
